  "body": "## Goal\n\nKeep the public FlipBot repository buildable while moving key Vinted conversation-inspection implementation into the private `jedreekPrograms/flipbot-playwright-core` repository.\n\n## Moved out of the public repository\n\nThe private core now owns:\n- live negotiation-event DOM classification,\n- seller counteroffer card scoping,\n- seller counteroffer plausibility checks,\n- read-only live item-price modal inspection,\n- seller-message/read-indicator DOM inspection,\n- Vinted-specific activity JavaScript.\n\nThe public repository keeps only orchestration, backend state, quotas/guards and a reflection bridge.\n\n## Runtime behavior\n\nThe real `FlipBotPlaywrightApplication` refuses to start without the private core implementation.\n\nOn an authorized Windows machine:\n\n```powershell\ncd playwright\n.\\bootstrap-private-core.ps1\n```\n\nThe script:\n1. clones/updates the private repository under `.private/`,\n2. runs its tests,\n3. installs its Maven artifact locally,\n4. creates the ignored `.private-core.enabled` marker,\n5. activates the private Maven dependency.\n\nNo GitHub token or private source is committed into the public repository.\n\n## Public CI\n\nThe public project compiles through `PrivateVintedCoreBridge` without a compile-time dependency on the private artifact. Vinted DOM implementation tests moved with the implementation into the private repository.\n\n## Safety preserved\n\nNo changes to:\n- daily quota / capacity,\n- persistent action guard / idempotency,\n- negotiation decision rules,\n- strategy snapshots/versioning,\n- terminal recovery,\n- scheduler ownership,\n- seller counter price semantics,\n- read/message/rejection timing policy.\n\nThe public orchestration still executes the same human-verification hook on every private-core poll.",
